  "body": "The release gate tier for v0.18.0 (branch `release/v0.18.0`, tree = main f490458a plus release docs and snapshot goldens; logs `gate-logs/release-20261112-001136/`) is green in 13 of 14 steps and red in one test of the app heavy lane (release, `--ignored`):\n\n```\ntest the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean ... FAILED\npanicked at crates\\app\\tests\\pocket3d_hsm.rs:100:5:\n[\"adaptive: the HSM plan for this area crosses itself at (-1.66, -2.80) - Offset rings cut the level at Z 20.000 instead\",\n \"adaptive: the HSM plan for this area crosses itself at (-1.99, -0.13) - Offset rings cut the level at Z 10.000 instead\"]\n```\n\nThe test pins (since #850 / PR #865) that on `testdata/models/Milling-test.step` only the TOP level (Z 20) falls back from the HSM plan to Offset rings, and the exact path size (5530 moves, 5497 planar feeds, 600 arcs). Now the Z 10 level falls back too. The toolpath still verifies clean (no warnings) and the fallback is named in the notes, so this is not wrong output: it is a quality regression on the user's own part - one more level cut with Offset rings instead of the adaptive plan.\n\nMost likely cause (to confirm by running the test at 575f02d8 and at its first parent): PR #839 (merged as 575f02d8) caps the STEP chord and so changes the imported mesh of this model; the level outline the planner works on is different. The heavy lane runs only at a cut, so nothing showed it when #839 merged. PR #865's review foresaw the tripwire (\"the bore test now asserts exact move counts on purpose\").\n\nTwo parts:\n1. For the cut: re-measure the pin and say why (the test's own comment asks for that), keeping every safety assertion - no warnings, each rings level named in the notes and the status line, no \"planning budget\" / \"too detailed\" refusal. Test-only.\n2. The real fix, after the cut: the Z 10 level of the bore gets its HSM plan back (why does the plan cross itself on the finer outline - near-duplicate vertices, a sliver, the arc fit of the outline?), or the reason it cannot is recorded.\n\nDone means: the Z 10 level of `Milling-test.step` is planned by the HSM planner again and the pin says `fell.len() == 1` again, or a decision entry explains why two levels is right; the heavy lane is green.\n",
